  "notes": "{慈|いつく}しむ expresses a deep, nurturing love directed toward someone or something vulnerable or precious.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: ～を{慈|いつく}しむ\n\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), む-ending.\n- Negative: {慈|いつく}しまない\n- Te-form: {慈|いつく}しんで\n- Past: {慈|いつく}しんだ\n- Noun form: {慈|いつく}しみ (tender love, compassion)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {子|こ}を{慈|いつく}しむ: to cherish one's child\n- {命|いのち}を{慈|いつく}しむ: to cherish life\n- {慈|いつく}しみの{心|こころ}: a heart of compassion\n- {慈|いつく}しみ{深|ぶか}い: deeply compassionate\n\nRELATED WORDS:\nThe kanji {慈|じ} means \"compassion\" or \"mercy\" and appears in:\n- {慈悲|じひ}: compassion, mercy (Buddhist term)\n- {慈善|じぜん}: charity, philanthropy\n- {慈愛|じあい}: affection, tender love",
